WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:06.480
We don't want you here that's the message
of around two hundred Tijuana residents protesting

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:10.270
the arrival of thousands of Central American
migrants.

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:12.960
The demonstration underlines the growing tension
here.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:18.000
The protestors accuse the migrants of forcing
their way into Mexico, and of being ungrateful

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.250
for the help they're offered.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.599
We don't want our government to support this
farce.

00:00:23.599 --> 00:00:29.980
We all know it's a sham.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:36.039
They're just bringing their problems here.

00:00:36.039 --> 00:00:47.750
They've just come here to use us.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:52.429
Our government is spending a lot of money
on them although there are many poor people

00:00:52.429 --> 00:00:54.160
here already.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:58.940
The protest march targeted the city's sports
stadium, which has been turned into a makeshift

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:00.859
shelter for the migrants.

00:01:00.859 --> 00:01:14.579
A police barrier kept them out, but the people
inside were trapped in the stadium all day.

00:01:14.579 --> 00:01:22.100
We're not leaving the stadium because we don't
want to instigate any violence.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:27.610
We fled violence and don't want to cause more
of it."

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:32.219
Locals threw stones at the migrants twice
in the last week.

00:01:32.219 --> 00:01:36.640
The people who arrived with the caravan are
frightened.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:37.640
Darío Suanso, migrante hondureño

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:38.820
We're in great danger.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:42.650
They come from areas of Mexico that don't
want us here.

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:47.799
They're disguised as garbage men, they're
armed and want to attack us.

00:01:47.799 --> 00:01:54.170
They hit a child on the head when they threw
stones at us.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:02:02.310
The flare-up of xenophobia in Mexican towns
along the migrants' route is unprecedented.

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:12.280
In Tijuana, locals are angry because the city
is ill-equipped to deal with the influx of

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:22.020
people -- who sleep on the streets and rely
on aid organisations for food.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:25.040
When someone is handing out chocolate everyone
crowds around.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:30.630
People are desperate, they've had a torturous
journey and do it to survive.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:36.690
There's no food in the shelters.

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:41.250
Racially charged comments from local politicians
have heightened tensions.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:48.800
A prominent example is Tijuana's Mayor Juan
Manuel Gastélum, who called the migrants

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:49.800
"lazy".

00:02:49.800 --> 00:03:03.450
A deputy of the state governor drove home
his law and order message at the protest:

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:09.220
Our government and society will welcome them
and help them, but only in keeping with the

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:10.950
law.

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:14.640
Residents here are very generous, but they
want rules to be upheld."

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:46.530
Such rhetoric has done nothing to cool the
hotheads on the streets of Tijuana.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:55.370
With more and more migrants crowding into
the city, there is plenty of scope for the

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:59.030
protests to grow.

